127392	127527	126864	126864	she	412	" I did . I told him plainly as words could tell him . ' Glencora , ' he said,--and you know the way he looks when he means to be lord and master , and put on the very husband indeed,--'This is an annoyance which you must bear and overcome . It suits me that we should go to Monkshade , and it does not suit me that there should be any one whom you are afraid to meet . ' Could I tell him that he would lose his wife if I did go ? Could I threaten him that I would throw myself into Burgo 's arms if that opportunity were given to me ? You are very wise , and very prudent . What would you have had me say ? "
